  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BUC">Lemma <span data-tag="0BUC">4.19.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{I}$ be a category. Let $\mathcal{J}$ be a full subcategory. Assume that $\mathcal{I}$ is filtered. Assume also that for any object $i$ of $\mathcal{I}$, there exists a morphism $i \to j$ to some object $j$ of $\mathcal{J}$. Then $\mathcal{J}$ is filtered and cofinal in $\mathcal{I}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
